## Architecture Overview

### Node-Based Relational Structure

```
node.json (Master Index)
   ├─→ node--service.json (node_id FK)
   │      └─→ category.json (category_id FK)
   │      └─→ review.json (service_id FK)
   │      └─→ rating.json (service_id FK)
   │
   ├─→ node--article.json (node_id FK)
   │      └─→ category.json (category_ids[] FK)
   │
   ├─→ comment.json (node_id FK)
   │
   └─→ review.json (node_id FK)
```

### Key Principles

1. **ID Management**: Auto-increment integers (like database)
2. **Slug**: URL-friendly identifier (separate from ID)
3. **Foreign Keys**: Relationships via numeric IDs
4. **Metadata Tracking**: Track last IDs in `_meta` objects
5. **Manual Edit**: Git-based workflow, manual JSON editing
6. **Type Safety**: Each node has a type (service, article, category)

